{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Which we ate in Egypt for free.</b> If you say that the Egyptians gave them fish for free — but was it not already said ״וְתֶבֶן לֹא יִנָּתֵן לָכֶם״ (Exodus 5)? If they did not give them straw for free, would they give them fish for free? And what does it mean by חִנָּם — free from the commandments (Sifrei)." "<b>The cucumbers.</b> Rabbi Shimon said: Why does the manna change into everything except these? Because they are harmful to nursing mothers — they say to a woman, do not eat garlic and onions because of the infant. A parable of a king, etc., as is found in Sifrei." "<b>The cucumbers.</b> These are קוקומבר\"ש בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>The melons.</b> בודיק\"ש." "<b>The leeks.</b> כְּרֵישִׁין; פוריל\"ש (Targum renders יָת בוֹצִינַיָּא, etc.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French cocombres, 'cucumbers'", 3 "the la'az lacks בְּלַעַ\"ז in this witness; Old French pomme de terre or similar, identifying the melon/watermelon", 4 "כְּרֵישִׁין is the Aramaic/Targumic equivalent (leeks); פוריל\"ש is Old French porreaux, 'leeks'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:22.202706461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}